WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:03.800
Now that we've all watched the first season
of The Boys, let's untangle all the plot threads

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.120
left dangling at the end of the season finale
and figure out where we stand with these comics-inspired

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.440
characters and their superpowered stories.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.400
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.500
The last we see of Hughie, he's helped his
teammates escape.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.600
He leaves Starlight behind at the warehouse
where they were being held, so she can try

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.780
to resuscitate A-Train.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.560
We don't know where Hughie's allies run to,
but so far they seem pretty adept at finding

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.860
hideouts when they need to.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.480
Hughie has grown in leaps and bounds.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:29.260
In spite of Butcher calling him "pathetic"
in the season finale because Hughie refuses

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.520
to help him kidnap Madelyn, the truth is Hughie
is as strong as any character in The Boys.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.830
He's grown from a young man still living with
his dad too afraid to ask for a raise at work

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:42.010
to an outlaw who murders a member of the world's
most prestigious superhero team, infiltrates

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.870
that same team's headquarters in a plot to
bug their conference room, and purposely gets

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.690
himself captured in the season finale so he
can rescue his new friends from what promises

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.860
to be torture and death.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.900
Yes, he yells "I'm sorry!" over and over as
he fires an assault rifle at the men guarding

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:55.580
Kimiko ...

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.900
"I'm sorry!

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.020
I'm Sorry!

00:00:59.320 --> 00:00:59.820
I'm out."

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.100
...but hey, a few episodes ago he was too
meek to tell his dad he didn't like pizza

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:04.600
rolls.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:05.640
Give the guy a break.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.540
Baby steps.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:10.760
Initially known simply as "The Female," the
powerful but silent Kimiko enjoys her own

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.110
evolution in this first season.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.220
When she's introduced in the fourth episode,
she's too wild and savage for anyone to leave

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:16.720
unbound.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:20.640
When Frenchie frees Kimiko, we see how physically
powerful she is and the violence of which

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.260
she's capable.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.190
We eventually learn Kimiko was kidnapped by
terrorists and used as a lab rat.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.160
At first, Kimiko won't even let Frenchie get
near her.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.120
But by the season finale, she's changed.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.020
She still isn't talking much, but the Boys
manage to win her trust, particularly Frenchie.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.820
Before the black ops team assaults the Boys'
motel room, she's cleaned herself up and put

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:41.250
on makeup, and she's clearly affected by the
young woman she sees in the mirror.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.940
We'll have to see if those changes have stuck
in season 2.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.480
Being recaptured may have thrown her back
into wild mode.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.880
Remember when we meet Kimiko she's a prisoner,
and in the space of five episodes she's captured

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:53.990
two more times, and nearly cut to pieces by
Black Noir.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:57.740
Repeatedly being captured and sliced open
probably doesn't promote emotional openness.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.360
Neither Mother's Milk nor Frenchie want to
be back working with Butcher when The Boys

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:02.920
begins.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.460
We haven't heard all the specifics yet, but
it's clear Butcher and the others once worked

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.640
with Mallory toward similar goals, and the
results weren't good.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:12.480
But more than that, neither of them want to
work with one another.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:16.500
Mother's Milk and Frenchie seem to have gallons
of bad blood between them, and no small part

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.720
of it seems to be due to Frenchie's attitude
toward Mother's Milk's wife.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.010
When Butcher recruits Mother's Milk he straight-up
lies about Frenchie's involvement and predictably

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.040
he has to pull the two apart when they see
each other.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.630
By the time they're imprisoned together in
the season finale, the warring outlaws have

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:30.720
made peace with one another.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.459
Perhaps it's because with Milk's wife in hiding
and telling him she never wants to see him

00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:36.590
again, neither of them have anything left
to lose.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.800
By the time he confronts Homelander, Butcher
is completely on his own.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:44.860
Hughie leaves him, and Butcher abandons the
rest of the team to their fate when he learns

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:45.360
they've been captured.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.420
Hearing about Homelander's twisted relationship
with Madelyn, Butcher goes to the executive's

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:53.200
house and covers her with explosives while
his finger rests on the dead man's switch.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.450
When things go sideways and Homelander kills
Madelyn himself, Butcher resigned to his fate

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:58.630
lets go of the switch.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:02.180
He wakes up in daylight on a green lawn, and
soon learns he's somewhere he could've never

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.160
imagined existed.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.640
Up until then, he believed that his wife Becca
was murdered by Homelander.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.620
In the season finale we learn at the same
time Butcher does Becca is alive and living

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:14.570
with an 8-year-old boy with blond hair and
eyes that glow red when Homelander tells him

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:15.060
who he is.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.640
How Butcher could possibly react to this is
anyone's guess.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:19.330
Will he be grateful his wife is alive?

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.640
Will that make him more or less committed
to taking down Homelander and Vought?

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.240
Not to mention, how's he going to survive
his confrontation with the leader of the Seven?

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:31.420
Elisabeth Shue is wonderful as the manipulative
and powerful Madelyn Stillwell, who somehow

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:35.560
not only pushes Vought to new levels of profit
but seems to be the only person who can exert

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.040
any control over Homelander.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.580
Unfortunately, Madelyn makes a fatal mistake.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.500
When referring to what supposedly happened
to Becca, she calls Homelander's child's death

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:47.730
a "miscarriage," alerting Homelander that
his lover and Jonah Vogelbaum didn't get their

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:48.640
stories straight.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:52.700
Just before he hollows out her skull with
his eyebeams, Homelander tells Madelyn he

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:56.680
"managed to squeeze" the truth out of Vogelbaum
that both mother and child survived.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.380
Save for Homelander himself, no character's
death could have more potential impact on

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.920
future seasons than Madelyn's.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:06.060
She may not have had superpowers, but throughout
the first season we learned just how important

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:06.900
Stillwell was.

00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:10.400
Not only was she the only person who could
rein in Homelander, she was pretty skilled

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.989
at manipulating the government officials who
stood in her way.

00:04:12.989 --> 00:04:17.449
Shortly before her death, Vought big cheese
Mr. Edgar makes it clear he sees her as his

00:04:17.449 --> 00:04:18.500
potential successor.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.520
With Madelyn gone, everything's up in the
air.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:24.539
Not to mention that both Vought and Homelander
will find themselves in a bind if they can't

00:04:24.539 --> 00:04:25.870
explain exactly how she died.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:31.169
In the beginning of The Boys, we get the notion
that Homelander is a powerful weapon but the

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:33.280
one pulling the trigger is Madelyn Stillwell.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.880
By the season finale, we've learned that isn't
quite true.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.260
When Homelander blasts the Baltimore mayor's
private plane out of the sky at the end of

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:43.120
the series premiere after the mayor blackmails
Madelyn it eventually comes to light that

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:45.020
Homelander was working all on his own.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:49.200
When a supe terrorist shows up in the season's
penultimate episode, it destroys the Boys'

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:49.700
plans.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.340
Even though Butcher had previously brought
a sample of the infamous Compound-V to the

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.300
CIA, the government isn't willing to go after
Vought because they need the corporation's

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.380
supes to fight these new super-powered enemies.

00:04:59.629 --> 00:05:02.660
While you could hardly be blamed for assuming
powering up terrorists was a company-wide

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:07.009
Vought conspiracy, we learn it was all Homelander's
plan to force the government to let superheroes

00:05:07.009 --> 00:05:08.160
work for the military.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:18.400
"And now we have villains all over the globe
that only we can fight."

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:23.500
Now, Madelyn is dead, Vought's supes are greenlit
for active service, and there is no one left

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:24.849
to keep Homelander in check.

00:05:24.849 --> 00:05:27.100
He was already the most physically powerful
man in the world.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:30.100
Now, Homelander is getting close to becoming
powerful in other ways.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:35.200
The last person that said “no” to Homelander
is dead, and at his hands - or eyes, whatever...

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:38.280
What happens if this twisted Superman stops
taking orders from Vought?

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:39.280
From the military?

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:39.780
From anyone?

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:44.539
We meet Dr. Stan Edgar for the first time
in the first season finale of The Boys.

00:05:44.539 --> 00:05:48.119
He gives Madelyn a bonus for helping get the
military contracts approved, and he makes

00:05:48.119 --> 00:05:50.819
it clear he's interested in her becoming his
successor.

00:05:50.819 --> 00:05:54.839
But Madelyn doesn't survive the season finale,
and it makes us wonder exactly how Vought

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.520
will recover from losing one of their most
effective executives.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:01.539
Without Stillwell, Vought's most powerful
and influential heroes will need a replacement

00:06:01.539 --> 00:06:05.090
handler, and that handler will have the challenge
of trying to control the physically most powerful

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:08.020
people in the world with fewer cards in their
hands than ever.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.539
Homelander has learned that he can not only
manipulate just as well as his dead lover,

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:14.000
but he can even kill Vought executives with
impunity.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.680
When a man can lift mountains and burn off
body parts by looking at them, what Vought

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:19.309
executive will be able to rein him in?

00:06:19.309 --> 00:06:22.440
And if no such person can be found, what happens
to Vought?

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:26.080
As Homelander pushes the envelope further
he's going to see Vought and the rest of the

00:06:26.089 --> 00:06:27.699
Seven as less and less important.

00:06:27.699 --> 00:06:31.690
By killing Madelyn, Homelander may have set
a time bomb within his own mind, and within

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:32.400
Vought itself.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:37.200
When we leave Starlight, she's acting more
like an actual superhero than any other member

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:37.840
of the Seven.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.420
A-Train would probably kill Hughie but his
heart gives out from his continued use of

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:45.999
Compound-V. Even though his survival could
mean her losing her spot on the team, imprisonment,

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:49.960
or even death, Starlight is performing CPR
on A-Train the last time we see her.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:54.500
A-Train knows Starlight helped Hughie escape,
and if he survives and tells Homelander, things

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:55.840
won't go well for Starlight.

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:57.160
There are other possibilities.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.479
A convenient if a bit predictable outcome
would be that A-Train survives but is unconscious

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:05.200
for a long time, can't remember what happened
right before his heart attack, or both.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:09.160
There's another potential outcome, and it
depends on exactly who Starlight has become.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:13.400
Earlier in the episode, Starlight has a conversation
with Queen Maeve, who tells Starlight she

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:17.199
was just as idealistic when she first joined
the Seven, but kept giving away pieces of

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.689
herself until there was nothing left.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:22.920
It's this conversation that convinces Starlight
to come to Hughie's aid, and it's a conversation

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:24.440
that may save A-Train's life.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:28.080
When Hughie leaves the warehouse, Starlight
could easily just stop trying to save A-Train's

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:28.580
life.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:32.400
Considering what's in store for her should
A-Train survive, the thought must be a tempting

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:32.900
one.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:36.580
If she gives in to that temptation, she may
get closer to the position Maeve has been

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:37.320
in for years.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:41.660
The Wonder-Woman-esque Queen Maeve is one
of the most conflicted characters we meet

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:42.400
in The Boys.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.419
She tells herself she gave up trying to be
a real hero long ago, but throughout the first

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:48.600
season we see glimpses of her desire to change.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:52.839
She tries and fails to get Homelander to save
at least some of the passengers of the doomed

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:54.560
Flight 37 in episode 4.

00:07:54.809 --> 00:07:59.160
Guilt-ridden over the event, she visits her
ex-girlfriend Elena but later rebukes her.

00:07:59.169 --> 00:08:03.129
When Homelander finds out about Hughie and
erroneously thinks Starlight helped him infiltrate

00:08:03.129 --> 00:08:05.820
Vought on purpose, it's Maeve who steps in
and defends her.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:09.860
"You want her, you got her.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.340
She's your responsibility now.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.840
I just hope you're right about her.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:15.140
For both of your sakes."

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:20.249
In the season finale, when Maeve finds a drunk
Starlight getting sick in the ladies' room,

00:08:20.249 --> 00:08:23.000
for the first time she shows genuine sympathy
for her teammate.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:26.680
Maeve opens up to the younger hero and tells
her that she really did care when she first

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:30.640
joined the Seven, but years of compromise
and giving away pieces of herself turned her

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:31.680
into something else.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:35.160
She urges Starlight to be herself, because
at least one of them should be.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:39.220
Whatever's coming in future seasons of The
Boys, Maeve may be the key element in any

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.760
struggles against Homelander.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:44.810
She clearly isn't ready for open revolt against
the more powerful supe, but she may very well

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:45.800
be getting close.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:49.160
By the season finale, the Deep has no allies
left.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:52.940
Homelander hates him for informing Madelyn
he's responsible for killing the Baltimore

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:53.440
mayor.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:58.100
He's exiled to the relatively crime-free Sandusky,
Ohio after his disastrous attempt to spring

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.440
a dolphin from a water park.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:03.411
All of this pales in comparison to the fact
that he forces himself on Starlight in the

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.300
premiere episode.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:08.520
In Sandusky, the Deep is even more useless
than ever and when word comes in that the

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.460
government has greenlit supes for military
action, he assumes his time for redemption

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:16.850
has come, but his Sandusky handler assures
him Vought wants the fish man to stay exactly

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:17.400
where he is.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.580
When we last see the Deep, he's freeing himself.

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:20.400
From hair.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:24.420
First he shaves all the hair off his chest,
and next he hesitantly buzzes all the hair

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:25.080
from his head.

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:26.420
So what is the Deep doing?

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.340
Well, what's one of the biggest differences
between a man and a fish?

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:30.000
Hair.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.180
Perhaps this low-rent Aquaman no longer sees
any options for himself on the surface world.

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:37.060
Maybe the Deep is planning to run away to
the place he's named after.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:41.560
He seems to have pretty stimulating conversations
with doomed dolphins and grocery store lobsters,

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.420
so who knows?

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:43.420
Maybe he'll be happy.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:45.080
"What's up man?

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:47.520
How'd you end up here?"

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:52.560
In the beginning of The Boys, Butcher and
Hughie are looking for vengeance.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:56.150
But by the end of the first season, it's clear
their quest may eventually have a much more

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:56.920
important goal.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:01.360
We now know that not only were the terrorist
supes exposed to Compound-V done so just so

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.700
the Seven would have an excuse to join the
military - but that it was Homelander who

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.500
was behind it all.

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:09.570
By the end of The Boys' first season, the
stakes have gone far beyond the profit margin

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.800
of Vought or violent emotional catharsis of
Butcher and Hughie.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:17.620
Homelander is now a threat on a global level.,
the ragtag team of revenge-seekers, mercenaries,

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:21.780
and traumatized lab rats may be the only thing
standing in the way of global annihilation.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:23.500
"This is never gonna stop!

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:27.020
It's just gonna be more blood and more awfulness.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:30.400
That's the f------ game."

